findings.fix:
N-006 cleanup:
- unregister the root;
- delete the tree, falling back to opening each placeholder with FILE_FLAG_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT and deleting it (the spike's manual fix);
- then assert the root is no longer registered and the folder is gone, failing the case otherwise (Q-176).

State the root's location explicitly: a fixed folder under the user's own %LOCALAPPDATA%\Temp when %TEMP% resolves to C:\WINDOWS\TEMP.

findings.claim:
The design's own lab-assay rule (no negative without a positive control) is not applied to its C3 open check. W-001 passes when no NothingListed row opens. If the checker's P/Invoke cannot open anything, every row 'stays refused' and the about-306,000-folder half of C3 passes vacuously, with nothing in the artefact to show it. Ways that can happen:
- a doubled \\?\ prefix;
- a wrong access or share constant;
- a missing SetLastError;
- a marshalling fault.

findings.fix:
In the same W-001 run, the checker must:
- open a known-listable folder (e.g. C:\Windows) and succeed;
- fail with 5 on a freshly planted deny-ListDirectory folder;
- succeed on a planted refused-then-listed folder (deny FILE_WRITE_ATTRIBUTES only).

The artefact records checkerControls{openable, denied, refusedThenListed}, and the verdict is inconclusive unless all three behave.

findings.claim:
The W-001 oracle treats any NothingListed row that opens now as a leak. It exempts only 363/REPARSE rows and code-2 folders recreated since the scan. The family is wider: any row whose cause has ended between the scan and the check fails a correct run. Members of the family:
- a code-32/33 holder that has since closed;
- a deny ACE that a concurrent worktree's WindowCases cleanup has since removed (U-110/U-112: 12-13 code-5 rows under Temp\fsa-window-cases on this PC);
- any ACL reset.

Only a code-5 row can be the leak C3 fears, because a refused keep-last-access open always records 5.

Rule 1's stated purpose is that no path reaches the schema-1 report from WindowReport. It guards only one route, the record ScanResult.Unreadable. WindowReport already reads list ItemsSource rows, and other routes to a path stay open:
- result.Store.GetPath(...);
- UnreadableList.ItemsSource or Items (UnreadableRow.Path);
- LargestFileRow and TopLevelRow members.

The settled-rule pattern on this project is to fence one API and miss its siblings (SL-056 learning).
